This license covers the original code in src/, examples/, linker/, and the
Makefile. It does not apply to:

- The third-party vendor SDKs pulled in under vendor/ (ARM CMSIS and
  STMicroelectronics cmsis-device-l4), which are separate projects
  distributed under their own Apache License 2.0 terms — see
  vendor/CMSIS/LICENSE.txt and vendor/STM32L4_Device/LICENSE.md after
  pulling them in (instructions in README.md).
- startup/startup_stm32l432xx.s, which is STMicroelectronics' own CMSIS
  startup file (copied unmodified from
  vendor/STM32L4_Device/Source/Templates/gcc/), also under Apache License
  2.0 per its embedded header.

The context-switch routines in src/sched.c (PendSV_Handler, SVC_Handler,
OS_start_tasks) were adapted from the FreeRTOS Cortex-M port, which is
MIT-licensed by Amazon Web Services, Inc.
